# Marlin-scoped presets (delivered via 92-variant-customizations.sh).
#
# Arch ships a disable-all default preset, and first-boot preset policy
# deletes enablement symlinks for units no preset names (see the shared
# 50-tunaos.preset header for the measured mechanism). These two units are
# enabled by 40-services.sh's pacman branch, so they are named here to
# preserve exactly what the build intends — scoped to marlin so no other
# variant's first-boot policy changes.
enable bluetooth.service
enable uupd.timer

# NetworkManager is the network stack on marlin. Arch's 90-systemd.preset
# enables systemd-networkd on first boot as well; networkd then manages no
# links (NetworkManager owns them all) and its wait-online unit times out
# after 2 minutes, delaying network-online.target and leaving the system
# degraded. 50- sorts before 90-, so these disables win. See #4522.
disable systemd-networkd.service
disable systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
disable systemd-networkd.socket
disable systemd-networkd-varlink.socket
